{"question_id": "Q3", "status": "UNRESOLVED", "document_code": "D004", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "split": "DEV", "title": "Microwave-Assisted Synthesis of Graphene–SnO2 Nanocomposites and Their Applications in Gas Sensors", "category": "ONTOLOGY_ENDPOINT_OR_PREDICATE_GAP", "annotation_scope": "SOURCE_CANDIDATE_ONLY_S4; NOT_A_COMPLETE_DOCUMENT_DRAFT", "evidence": [{"span_id": "0089ac36-0f2b-511e-9fcf-cc6f0af9d17f", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 444, "end": 647, "text": "By the microwave treatment of graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites, with the graphene promoting efficient transport of the microwave energy, evaporation and redeposition of SnO x nanoparticles were facilitated.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}], "context": [{"span_id": "5557eb41-a08a-51e7-8386-e4d83fb8e302", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 350, "end": 443, "text": "The overall oxygen atomic ratio was decreased with the appearance of an SnO x ( x < 2) phase.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "e17663da-498a-5a50-b70e-37f32682a02e", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 648, "end": 784, "text": "The graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites exhibited a high sensor response of 24.7 for 1 ppm of NO 2 gas, at an optimized temperature of 150 °C.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}], "candidate_mentions": [{"mention_id": "6ad3cfb4-9084-5503-82d0-18c16d638f75", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "surface_text": "microwave treatment of graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites", "start": 451, "end": 503, "kind": "PROCESS", "contextual_role": "technical_process", "canonical_concept": "49871fe1-4cdd-5db2-befa-08ae901dd56c", "coreference_group": null, "evidence_span_ids": ["5016af0e-838e-5037-9144-7ad6c7da00e4"], "annotation_status": "AI_DRAFT", "local_key": "treatment", "sentence_id": "S4"}, {"mention_id": "d1f1a0cb-16ad-5e36-806b-b8389e7da3e6", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "surface_text": "graphene", "start": 514, "end": 522, "kind": "MATERIAL", "contextual_role": "energy_transport_promoter", "canonical_concept": "cc37c952-e478-51af-be9b-35d80c46a5f3", "coreference_group": null, "evidence_span_ids": ["eb487021-894f-548c-b7dd-d23fb73aebd0"], "annotation_status": "AI_DRAFT", "local_key": "graphene", "sentence_id": "S4"}, {"mention_id": "9deb6ab8-b26e-505c-857a-c96cb6f51d15", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "surface_text": "efficient transport of the microwave energy", "start": 533, "end": 576, "kind": "PROCESS", "contextual_role": "technical_process", "canonical_concept": "c1a4aadd-9d4b-5889-a0b5-518aef0e86fd", "coreference_group": null, "evidence_span_ids": ["cf7ec443-e02d-5183-a20c-dad847e05347"], "annotation_status": "AI_DRAFT", "local_key": "transport", "sentence_id": "S4"}, {"mention_id": "3cc52b1d-8fce-5d45-b642-f9cb229895b6", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "surface_text": "evaporation and redeposition of SnO x nanoparticles", "start": 578, "end": 629, "kind": "PROCESS", "contextual_role": "technical_process", "canonical_concept": "cc163d15-bf3c-50aa-9adb-8794cb66d117", "coreference_group": null, "evidence_span_ids": ["7e702040-6518-52fe-a25a-489023b216c3"], "annotation_status": "AI_DRAFT", "local_key": "evap_redeposit", "sentence_id": "S4"}], "candidate_concepts": [{"concept_id": "49871fe1-4cdd-5db2-befa-08ae901dd56c", "canonical_name": "microwave treatment", "kind": "PROCESS", "instance_scope": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "normalization_version": "pilot24-dev-rubric-0.2-WORKING"}, {"concept_id": "cc37c952-e478-51af-be9b-35d80c46a5f3", "canonical_name": "graphene", "kind": "MATERIAL", "instance_scope": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "normalization_version": "pilot24-dev-rubric-0.2-WORKING"}, {"concept_id": "c1a4aadd-9d4b-5889-a0b5-518aef0e86fd", "canonical_name": "microwave energy transport", "kind": "PROCESS", "instance_scope": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "normalization_version": "pilot24-dev-rubric-0.2-WORKING"}, {"concept_id": "cc163d15-bf3c-50aa-9adb-8794cb66d117", "canonical_name": "SnOx evaporation/redeposition process group", "kind": "PROCESS", "instance_scope": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "normalization_version": "pilot24-dev-rubric-0.2-WORKING"}], "candidate_evidence_spans": [{"span_id": "a8992bfb-66ea-5534-ac34-d2ff616aa8aa", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 0, "end": 144, "text": "We obtained extremely high and selective sensitivity to NO 2 gas by fabricating graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites using a commercial microwave oven.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "17757883-97ff-5e52-a5bd-9599e1d475b3", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 145, "end": 349, "text": "Structural characterization revealed that the products corresponded to agglomerated structures of graphene and SnO 2 particles, with small secondary SnO x ( x ≤ 2) nanoparticles deposited on the surfaces.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "5557eb41-a08a-51e7-8386-e4d83fb8e302", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 350, "end": 443, "text": "The overall oxygen atomic ratio was decreased with the appearance of an SnO x ( x < 2) phase.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "0089ac36-0f2b-511e-9fcf-cc6f0af9d17f", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 444, "end": 647, "text": "By the microwave treatment of graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites, with the graphene promoting efficient transport of the microwave energy, evaporation and redeposition of SnO x nanoparticles were facilitated.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "e17663da-498a-5a50-b70e-37f32682a02e", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 648, "end": 784, "text": "The graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites exhibited a high sensor response of 24.7 for 1 ppm of NO 2 gas, at an optimized temperature of 150 °C.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "8235f76e-6dae-58c7-8e00-d9786f6e3272", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 785, "end": 908, "text": "The graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites were selectively sensitive to NO 2 gas, in comparison with SO 2, NH 3, and ethanol gases.", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "e4753075-93f4-5ca0-8d11-fded24cdfedb", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "eb47e91a-4c35-4de7-96a3-f141eea0a6cf", "start": 0, "end": 321, "text": "We suggest that the generation of SnO x nanoparticles and the SnO x phase in the matrix results in the formation of SnO 2 /SnO 2 homojunctions, SnO 2 /SnO x ( x < 2) heterojunctions, and SnO 2 /graphene heterojunctions, which are responsible for the excellent sensitivity of the graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites to NO 2 gas.", "source_text_sha256": "4fb5907a3a82cde6bcf412375e3883c2c52a669235fec58ce11b70619222a212"}, {"span_id": "6617ab9b-00a2-5290-abbe-bc5cf9eed310", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "eb47e91a-4c35-4de7-96a3-f141eea0a6cf", "start": 322, "end": 478, "text": "In addition, the generation of surface Sn interstitial defects is also partly responsible for the excellent NO 2 sensing performance observed in this study.", "source_text_sha256": "4fb5907a3a82cde6bcf412375e3883c2c52a669235fec58ce11b70619222a212"}, {"span_id": "5016af0e-838e-5037-9144-7ad6c7da00e4", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 451, "end": 503, "text": "microwave treatment of graphene–SnO 2 nanocomposites", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "eb487021-894f-548c-b7dd-d23fb73aebd0", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 514, "end": 522, "text": "graphene", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "cf7ec443-e02d-5183-a20c-dad847e05347", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 533, "end": 576, "text": "efficient transport of the microwave energy", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}, {"span_id": "7e702040-6518-52fe-a25a-489023b216c3", "document_id": "08d58bd1-a89e-4b70-b817-821df8428bc7", "revision_id": "5afc0eeb-3c76-40cf-99be-e70f066beb2b", "chunk_id": "1314b88d-a703-48b5-bb03-e426d5474034", "start": 578, "end": 629, "text": "evaporation and redeposition of SnO x nanoparticles", "source_text_sha256": "5ab47cc03efc60802c5c6bece098307c9084b5e327212580366207ab757116c9"}], "candidates": [{"head_mention_id": "d1f1a0cb-16ad-5e36-806b-b8389e7da3e6", "tail_mention_id": "9deb6ab8-b26e-505c-857a-c96cb6f51d15", "proposed_relation_type": "FACILITATES", "modality": "ASSERTED", "polarity": "POSITIVE", "support_status": "UNRESOLVED", "reason": "Explicit promotion/facilitation of a process; accepted IMPROVES has no MATERIAL head or PROCESS tail."}, {"head_mention_id": "6ad3cfb4-9084-5503-82d0-18c16d638f75", "tail_mention_id": "3cc52b1d-8fce-5d45-b642-f9cb229895b6", "proposed_relation_type": "FACILITATES", "modality": "ASSERTED", "polarity": "POSITIVE", "support_status": "UNRESOLVED", "reason": "Explicit promotion/facilitation of a process; accepted IMPROVES has no MATERIAL head or PROCESS tail."}], "human_review": "NOT_REVIEWED", "ontology_change_applied": false}
